        "assistantId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "={{ $json.assistant_id }}",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "prompt": "define",
        "text": "=Using the audience database stored in the system, generate 3 distinct audiences for the given buyer persona and product. Please follow the instructions below and maintain the variable structures as provided.\n\n{{ $json.product_details }}\n\n{{ $json.buyer_person_details }}\n\nAudience Generation\n\nGenerate 3 different audiences that align with \"{{ $json.product_name }}\" and \"{{ $json.buyer_person_name }}\":\n\n- Audience 1: Hyper-Segmented \n  A highly specific, niche audience.\n- Audience 2: Segmented\n  A moderately broad audience.\n- Audience 3: Broad\n  A more general audience.\n\nThe output is a correct formed JSON array that contains the generated elements, in this form:\n\n[ \n  <Element Generated 1>,<Element Generated 2>, .. , <Element Generated N>\n]\n\nEach one of these elements must replicate this structure\n\n{\n  \"AudienceSegment\": \"Audience 1\",\n  \"Audience\": \"High-Income Male Professionals in Downtown Mexico City\",\n  \"Demographics\": {\n    \"Age\": \"33-37 years old\",\n    \"Gender\": \"Male\",\n    \"Location\": [\n      \"Downtown Mexico City\",\n      \"Business District ZIP Codes\"\n    ],\n    \"IncomeLevel\": \"Top 5% income households\"\n  },\n  \"Interests\": [\n    \"Investments\",\n    \"Personal Finance\",\n    \"Luxury Goods\",\n    \"Luxury Travel\",\n    \"Investment Banking\"\n  ]\n}\n\nPlease, omit any introductory comment previously to the answer, go directly to the output, and remove from response json tag.",
        "options": {}
      },
